            "review_title": "Review at Belgica",
            "review_text": "Luis Henrique N\nColombo, Sri Lanka16 contributions\n0\nNEGLECT\nJun 2022 • Couples\n2nd June I and my wife visited an apparently cozy and cool place in Saigon called Belgica. Nice music and decoration, English speaking staff, Belgian beer and many other items in the menu showing variety and creativity.\n We chose a table and quickly a young waiter approached us and took our order: fried calamari as appetisers, two mugs of black ale, one lime juice and finally fish and salad.\n Then, a colleague of his came to us again, confirmed our request and soon brought drinks, and calamari, and there we remained enjoying the first part of our meal. To remark that it was around 8:40 PM and being supposed to have an important phone call at 10 PM, my wife had calculated the exact time for a calm dinner. \n Time went by, two more mugs of beer were served, conversation over them continued till 9:20 PM approximately. In order not to be rushed for eating, we finally asked to have our order parcelled, so as to enjoy it as take away. \n Finally came the big news: the same guy who had initially confirmed our order told us that, according to the cook, it was only appetisers and beer. Given the absurdity of the situation we simply asked for the bill, despite the several apologies expressed by that guy - never the first one reappeared - and offer of having our order expedited. A westerner waiter took the same attitude and gave us 2 extra mugs of beer for free , as if this could compensate the burden such a staff had created to us. We accepted his offer, anyhow and hope a serious conversation was had with the staff there, where high prices not necessarily carry high quality in services. Belgica is definitely a place to be second/third place considered when it comes to have any meal in Saigon.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 2, 2022",
